==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|biutel}}, from {{inh|de|goh|būtil}}. Cognate with {{cog|nl|buidel}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈbɔʏ̯təl/|[ˈbɔø̯tl̩]|lang=de}}
* {{audio|De-Beutel.ogg|Audio|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m||Beutel}}

# a small to medium-sized [[bag]], usually of fabric
#: {{ux|de|Der '''Beutel''' ist ziemlich voll.|The bag is quite full.}}
# [[pouch]] {{gloss|bag with a [[drawstring]]}}
# [[pouch]] {{gloss|body part of a [[marsupial]]}}

====Usage notes====
* Bags of paper or plastic are more properly called {{m|de|Tüte|Tüten}}, though {{m|de||Beutel}} can be used as well. Moreover, only {{m|de||Beutel}} is used in some particular contexts, e.g. {{m|de|Staubsaugerbeutel|t=vacuum cleaner bag}}, {{m|de|Teebeutel|t=tea bag}}, etc.

